{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command 'Get-Content docs/work/active/wi-982/WI-982-minted-row-carries-authoring-tags.md; Get-Content docs/rubrics/kit-change-review.md; git diff de3838360df865666872aa4520ca66d6c8233471...a86e826877d289bdd698e88b59b4b97cb8eecd43 -- project-trajectory/scripts project-trajectory/registries/work-items.template.csv docs/requirements docs/test/test-cases.toml docs/registry-machinery-reference.md project-trajectory/RESYNC_PACK.md tests'","aggregated_output":"+++\r\nid = \"WI-982\"\r\ntitle = \"Both adjudication routes widen a sitting's hats by the authoring work item's tags: the minted first-approval and amendment rows carry the merged lane's tags\"\r\nworkstream = \"process\"\r\nsr_refs = [\"SR-161\"]\r\nspecref = \"docs/reviews/wi-976/004-ADJUDICATE-81e623b.md\"\r\nbuildtier = \"medium\"\r\nsafety_class = \"ordinary\"\r\npriority = 5\r\nplanmode = \"single\"\r\n+++\r\n\r\n## Context\r\n\r\nFiled by hand by headless leg 23 (2026-10-26) at WI-976's landing, from\r\nthe SUCCESSOR ruling of WI-976's dispute sitting 004\r\n(`docs/reviews/wi-976/004-ADJUDICATE-81e623b.md`, RB1-F1, accepted; its\r\nduplicate RB3-F1 was dismissed by sitting 010, and the post-rebase round's\r\nREVIEW-B re-raised the same class, `docs/decisions/wi-976.toml` D-028).\r\n\r\nWhat is true: a decomposition round's hats are widened by the tags of the\r\nrow the sitting composer is handed. The coordinator's in-lane route hands\r\nit the authoring lane's own row. The unattended route hands it the\r\nmerge-minted adjudication row, whose Workstream is always `process` and\r\nwhose SafetyClass is `adjudication` (it routes the row), so the authoring\r\nwork item's tags are lost and the hat set differs by route. The defect is\r\nin the minted row's provenance, outside WI-976's declared surface.\r\n\r\nThe ruling, verbatim: \"make both routes widen a sitting's parent needs by\r\nthe authoring work item's declared tags: carry the merged lane's\r\nWorkstream and SafetyClass (in a cell other than the routing SafetyClass)\r\nor a link to it onto every minted first-approval and amendment row,\r\nresolve the branchless sweep, state in LLR-360 that the authoring work\r\nitem's tags widen, and add a test that composes the minted row shape and\r\nthe in-lane shape for one SR and asserts one hat set\".\r\n\r\nIts scope critique runs before its claim (the `coordinator-cycle` skill,\r\nsection 1).\r\n\r\n**Deliverables and order (S1).** Two deliverables, kept together in one\r\nlanding on purpose: the mint writing the provenance cell and the composer\r\nreading it, with the paired-shape test. A cell nothing reads changes no\r\nhat, and a reader with no writer reads nothing, so neither lands first.\r\nThe ruling's LLR-360 item needs no work: that row already reads \"widens\r\neach need by the authoring work item's declared tags\", and this row leaves\r\nthe clause standing.\r\n\r\n**Architectural delta (S5).** No new mode class and no new boundary. The\r\nrow adds one cell, `authoring_tags`, to the work-item row\r\n(`wi_convert.COLUMNS`, the schema IF-092 names, in the IF-023 carrier). Its\r\nvalue domain: the authoring work items' Workstream and SafetyClass values,\r\ndeduplicated and `;`-joined, or empty when no authoring item is known. The\r\nruling's alternative, a link, is not taken: the mint already holds the\r\nrows, so it writes the fact once and a later composition reads that record\r\ninstead of looking a row up (rubric B3). `intake`'s two drafters are the\r\nonly writers. `hats.context_from_work_item` is the only reader: a non-empty\r\ncell supplies the row's tags in place of its Workstream and SafetyClass,\r\nnever beside them, since beside them a minted row would keep `process` and\r\nits FIRST-RUN-ADOPTER hat and the sets would still differ. An empty cell\r\nreads those two cells, as every row does today, so the in-lane route\r\nchanges nothing. The output that moves is the hat set, which now depends\r\non the authoring tags on both routes. The routing SafetyClass stays\r\n`adjudication`.\r\n\r\n**Provenance cases (S3).** The cell's source is closed, by the route that\r\nmints:\r\n\r\n- The merge slot: the lane's closed row, the one its outcomes name.\r\n- `sweep --merged ... --branch`: the named rows, their tags unioned when\r\n  there are several.\r\n- A range sweep with no `--merged`, with or without `--with-terminal`: the\r\n  branchless case. It knows no authoring item (`--branch` alone only labels\r\n  the commit, and `--with-terminal` holds every close on file), so the\r\n  default applies: the cell stays empty and the row widens by its own tags,\r\n  as a minted row does today. A person who knows the lane gets its tags by\r\n  naming its rows with `--merged`.\r\n- A bare sweep: it reads HEAD..HEAD, so it mints neither row kind.\r\n\r\nAn authoring row's tags are the ones it widens by itself, so a minted row\r\nthat authors another passes its cell on. No route infers a lane from\r\nhistory. The promise reaches what these routes mint (PROCESS.md §6,\r\n\"Review threat model\"); a hand-edited cell is outside it.\r\n\r\n## Done-when\r\n\r\n- [ ] Every first-approval and amendment row minted by a route that names\r\n      an authoring work item carries that item's Workstream and\r\n      SafetyClass in `authoring_tags`, a cell other than the routing\r\n      SafetyClass.\r\n- [ ] The branchless sweep's case is resolved as \"Provenance cases\" states:\r\n      a range sweep with no `--merged` leaves the cell empty, its row\r\n      widens by its own tags, and a test pins it.\r\n- [ ] Both routes widen a sitting's parent needs by the authoring work\r\n      item's declared tags wherever that item is named, and LLR-360 states\r\n      that it is the authoring work item's tags that widen.\r\n- [ ] A test composes the minted row shape and the in-lane shape for one\r\n      SR and asserts one hat set.\r\n- [ ] The commit bar is green, and both strict lints are clean on the\r\n      landing tip.\r\n\r\n## Critique dispositions\r\n\r\nRound 1 (fresh Sol, 2026-11-04): CHANGES-REQUESTED, one MAJOR and three\r\nMINORs.\r\n\r\n- **S1, adopted.** The Context now reads \"Two deliverables, kept together\r\n  in one landing on purpose\", and records that LLR-360 \"already reads\".\r\n- **S3, adopted.** The unresolved bullet is replaced. \"Provenance cases\"\r\n  reads \"The cell's source is closed, by the route that mints\", its\r\n  branchless default reads \"the cell stays empty and the row widens by its\r\n  own tags\", and its bound reads \"The promise reaches what these routes\r\n  mint\". The first and third Done-when bullets are narrowed to match.\r\n- **S4, adopted.** The frontmatter reads `planmode = \"single\"`: the row\r\n  touches the mint and the hat composer, and promises behaviour over the\r\n  mint's routes.\r\n- **S5, adopted.** The delta reads \"No new mode class and no new boundary\",\r\n  names the carrier's domain (\"deduplicated and `;`-joined, or empty when\r\n  no authoring item is known\"), its writers and its one reader, and states\r\n  that the hat set \"now depends on the authoring tags on both routes\".\r\n# Rubric — Reviewing a change to this kit (WI-852)\r\n\r\n**Adjudicates:** the checks a review of a change to this repository owes beyond\r\nthe kit's reviewer brief, which already asks for the failure classes, the\r\nDone-when coverage map, the red-before test, the unrepresentable clause and the\r\nrequirement-row sweep.\r\n**Used by:** an independent reviewer of a lane, when its brief is rendered with\r\n`review_brief.py review --rubric docs/rubrics/kit-change-review.md`.\r\n\r\n## Intent\r\n\r\nThe rules this repository holds its own lanes to (`CLAUDE.md`, and the owner\r\nrulings the spine-authoring skill records) that the kit's shipped brief cannot\r\nname, because an adopter's repository has its own.\r\n\r\n## Anchors\r\n\r\n**K1 — Requirement text is true, and the right way round.** Read every added or\r\namended SN, SR, LLR and TC cell against PROCESS.md and the code. *Bad:* a row\r\nstating the inverse of the rule its code implements; earlier waves shipped\r\nthat, and code review missed it.\r\n\r\n**K2 — Owner ruling R2, as review-churn ruling 5 refines it.** No SN or SR\r\ncell names an implementation carrier (a script, command, file or function),\r\nacceptance included. Current-carrier evidence lives in the TC rows that verify\r\nthe row, and a shipped boundary artifact (a registry, template, config file or\r\nlauncher) may be named at the LLR and TC tiers only. An approved cell keeps its\r\napproved text, names included, until it is amended through its authority.\r\n\r\n**K3 — Back-links and approved rows.** Each `Implements:` tag names the LLR\r\nwhose `module` is that file, and the function appears in that LLR's\r\n`code_symbol`. An approved row changes only where the spec grants it, and no\r\nStatus flips.\r\n\r\n**B1 — A finding stated as a guess.** Report a finding as a claim confirmed by\r\nreading or running the code, never as a guess.\r\ndiff --git a/docs/registry-machinery-reference.md b/docs/registry-machinery-reference.md\nindex 3b97b1efe..9ebd09306 100644\n--- a/docs/registry-machinery-reference.md\n+++ b/docs/registry-machinery-reference.md\n@@ -877,6 +877,37 @@ The brief renders BOTH the recorded pair and the pair as the tree stands\n a number with nothing to compare against — the slot exists so a stale verdict is\n detectable rather than assumed fresh.\n \n+### The `AuthoringTags` cell — whose tags a sitting widens by\n+\n+A minted first-approval or amendment row always carries `Workstream = process`\n+and the routing `SafetyClass = adjudication`, so those two cells say how the row\n+routes, not what its authoring work item was. `AuthoringTags` holds that fact:\n+the authoring work items' `Workstream` and `SafetyClass` values, deduplicated\n+and `;`-joined, or empty when no authoring item is known. `intake`'s two drafters\n+are its only writers, and a `## Dispositions` block declaring the key is refused\n+as unknown. `hats.context_from_work_item` is its only reader: a non-empty cell\n+supplies the row's tags in place of the two cells, never beside them, and an\n+empty cell reads the two cells.\n+\n+| Route | Source | Cell |\n+|---|---|---|\n+| merge slot | the closed rows its `outcomes` name | their tags |\n+| `sweep --merged ... --branch` | the named rows | their union, in sorted-id order |\n+| range sweep with no `--merged`, with or without `--with-terminal` or `--branch` | none | empty |\n+| bare sweep | none, and it reads HEAD..HEAD | mints neither row kind |\n+\n+The route test is `branch`, not `outcomes`: `--with-terminal` hands every close\n+on file, and only the routes that name their rows hand a claim branch. An\n+authoring row's tags are read through the same function, so a minted row that\n+authors another passes its cell on. A row already minted keeps its cell, so a\n+later `--merged` sweep over a range already minted writes nothing.\n+\n+It is a REAL COLUMN for the reason `Supersedes` and `Brief` share: `intake` writes\n+it through `wi_convert.write_spec_file`, which serializes from\n+`wi_convert.COLUMNS`, and a frontmatter key outside that table is dropped by\n+`parse_spec`. A column also lets a later composition read the recorded fact\n+instead of looking a row up.\n+\n **Chain-consistency warns — RETIRED** (owner ruling 2026-08-17, the cell\n reading): `modified_chain_advisories` told an author to flip the owning SR\n whenever a child read the retired `Modified` marker, asserting the retired\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/interfaces.toml b/docs/requirements/interfaces.toml\nindex 0c854d9f3..0c3947020 100644\n--- a/docs/requirements/interfaces.toml\n+++ b/docs/requirements/interfaces.toml\n@@ -1292,7 +1292,7 @@ component = \"CMP-008\"\n owner = \"scripts/wi_convert\"\n requestors = [\"scripts/intake\"]\n channel = \"call\"\n-data = \"wi_convert.COLUMNS (the 19-column row schema) and write_spec_file; ConvertError is the mint's refusal input\"\n+data = \"wi_convert.COLUMNS with AuthoringTags (authoring tags, ;-joined, or empty) and write_spec_file; ConvertError is the mint's refusal input\"\n version = \"v1\"\n status = \"Drafted\"\n component = \"CMP-008\"\ndiff --git a/docs/requirements/low-level-requirement
