{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_24","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command \"Get-Content scripts/coordinator/compose_lane.py | Select-Object -First 165; rg -n 'authoring|tags|classification|Workstream|SafetyClass' docs/requirements/interfaces.toml | Select-Object -First 16; git diff --exit-code -- docs/test/report.md\"","aggregated_output":"\"\"\"compose_lane.py — compose an in-lane adjudication brief (wave-10 recipe).\r\n\r\nRun FROM THE LANE ROOT with the repo venv:\r\n\r\n    python \"$TOOLS/compose_lane.py\" \\\r\n        WI-NNN <brief> \"<ID;ID;...>\" \"<SR;SR>\" <verdict-path> <out.md>\r\n\r\n<brief> is the adjudication kind the merge would mint (`amendment` or\r\n`first-approval`); the row is the lane's own work-item row with `Brief`,\r\n`Adjudicates` and `SR-Refs` overridden, exactly as the coordinator composed\r\nWI-688's and WI-787's briefs. The kit's own `adjudicate_brief.compose` fills\r\nit, so the adjudicator reads the brief the merge's mint would hand a sitting.\r\n\"\"\"\r\n\r\nimport sys\r\nfrom pathlib import Path\r\n\r\nsys.path.insert(0, \"project-trajectory/scripts\")\r\nimport adjudicate_brief  # noqa: E402\r\nimport consolidate  # noqa: E402\r\n\r\n\r\ndef main(argv):\r\n    wi, brief, scope, srs, verdict, out = argv\r\n    root = Path(\".\").resolve()\r\n    rows = {r[\"WI-ID\"]: r for r in consolidate.read_rows(root)}\r\n    if wi not in rows:\r\n        print(\"compose_lane: no row {} under {}\".format(wi, root))\r\n        return 2\r\n    row = dict(rows[wi])\r\n    row[\"Brief\"] = brief\r\n    row[\"Adjudicates\"] = scope\r\n    row[\"SR-Refs\"] = srs\r\n    body, why = adjudicate_brief.compose(root, row, verdict)\r\n    if body is None:\r\n        print(\"compose_lane: REFUSED: {}\".format(why))\r\n        return 1\r\n    Path(out).write_text(body, encoding=\"utf-8\", newline=\"\\n\")\r\n    print(\"compose_lane: {} {} -> {} ({} chars)\".format(wi, brief, out, len(body)))\r\n    return 0\r\n\r\n\r\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\r\n    sys.exit(main(sys.argv[1:]))\r\n427:data = \"skills/INDEX.csv: banner comment, header, one row per skill (name, scope, stacks, domains, phases, tags, description)\"\r\n683:data = \"SKILL.md frontmatter: name, scope, stacks, domains, phases, tags; each other file in the skill directory, materialized with it at the same relative path\"\r\n1295:data = \"wi_convert.COLUMNS with AuthoringTags (authoring tags, ;-joined, or empty) and write_spec_file; ConvertError is the mint's refusal input\"\r\n1668:notes = \"The digest uses the same approved-cell classification as split_changed_cells, so a carrier representation and an absent versus empty cell do not change it.\"\r\n1675:data = \"scan_inventory, contracts_grammar_findings, file_contracts, file_grammar_findings, owner_files, ContractsGrammarError, read_test_tags\"\r\n2092:rationale = \"\"\"A reviewer starting from an outcome needs to see what it relies on and whether any of it has been shown false, and neither the per-assumption reports nor the approval brief starts from a need. Deriving the view from the registries in the dashboard's source layer, through the same classification rule the checker applies, keeps it from going stale the way a hand-written summary does and keeps the page and the checker agreeing.\"\"\"\r\n2406:data = \"architecture inventories and findings for seams, contracts, components, code symbols, spec boundaries, and test-file tags\"\r\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
