{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_27","type":"command_execution","command":"\"C:\\\\Program Files\\\\PowerShell\\\\7\\\\pwsh.exe\" -Command '$reviewText = @'\"'\nReviewed: a86e826877d289bdd698e88b59b4b97cb8eecd43\n\nVerified: Independently reviewed the scoped three-dot diff, AGENTS.md/CLAUDE.md, PROCESS.md sections 3/5/6, WI-982's complete spec and cited owner ruling, and rubric K1/K2/K3/B1. Hunted silent loss of authoring tags first, then unintended routing/approval changes and inconsistent route behavior. Real intake and sweep flows preserve authoring tags separately from routing, union only named authors, propagate a minted author's tags, and leave unnamed sweeps at the specified fallback. Full adjudicate_brief.compose calls on a real minted row and the in-lane shape both include UNATTENDED-OPS and exclude FIRST-RUN-ADOPTER. No attributable defect found. The sole prescribed pytest failure reproduces on baseline behavior with the same Git-for-Windows CreateFileMapping access error; the complete test command therefore was not green in this environment.\n\nRequirement/interface semantic decisions: LLR-360's changed Module/CodeSymbol trace cells and IF-092's changed schema description correspond to the new writer/reader path and TC-399's added Verifies/Evidence links; carry those changes together. Retain LLR-360 Detail and SR-161 Requirement/AcceptanceCriteria because they already require widening by the authoring item's tags and every applicable perspective. Retain IF-023 because it specifies the per-row Markdown carrier rather than an exhaustive field list. Retain TC-399 Method/Expected because their existing work-item widening and per-perspective outcomes remain the behavioral obligation; the added evidence exercises its provenance and schema seam. This is a coverage-gap correction under PROCESS section 5, not preservation of an unsuitable LLR. Parent acceptance and approval are unchanged, enduring tests remain, and no Status flip is introduced. This review records semantic endorsement, not a substitute approval-ledger act. Targeted sweeps of existing SR-161/SN-036, their related requirement rows, LLR-360, IF-023/IF-092 and citing TC rows found no newly introduced contradiction, overlap or limit conflict. No decomposition is introduced. The new helper centralizes author selection and reuses the existing tag reader; no repeated implementation found.\n\nDone-when coverage:\n- D1: test_the_slot_mint_carries_the_closed_lanes_tags_on_both_row_kinds covers first-approval and amendment; test_a_merged_sweep_unions_the_named_rows_tags covers explicit multi-author sweep; test_a_minted_author_passes_its_cell_on covers inherited provenance; converter and loader tests cover durable storage.\n- D2: test_a_range_sweep_with_no_merged_leaves_the_cell_empty_and_widens_by_its_own_tags covers plain range, --with-terminal and --branch alone; test_a_bare_sweep_mints_neither_row_kind covers the bare case.\n- D3: reader tests cover both column and frontmatter forms and empty fallback; test_the_authoring_cell_widens_each_need_and_sibling_needs_never_merge covers independent parent widening. LLR-360 Detail already names the authoring work item. Full composer calls verify the shipped brief path.\n- D4: test_a_real_mint_and_the_lane_row_compose_one_hat_set compares the two shapes for one SR; independent full composer calls confirm the actual briefs carry the correct questions.\n- D5: prescribed targeted bar completed with 304 passed, 4 skipped and one baseline-reproduced host failure; both strict lints passed. An entirely green bar remains unverified in this environment, with no range-induced failure observed.\n\nTest adequacy: New behavior tests exercise the row converter, public context/composition functions, intake_after_merge and the sweep CLI rather than inspecting handler source. Nine parameterized new-behavior cases failed at assertions with the corresponding exact baseline function/module implementations restored in memory: two slot kin